{"schema":1,"function":"gamma_ppf","description":"Gamma distribution quantile function, the x with P(a, x) = p (shape a, rate 1); half the chi-squared quantile with df = 2a","inputs":["a","p"],"outputs":["y"],"points":432,"tolerance":{"rel":2e-13,"reason":"p and a are exact doubles and 1 - p is exact for p >= 1/2, but in the lower tail the quantile is x = exp(L) with L = (log p + log Gamma(a + 1)) / a approximately; rounding L (or 1/a, which multiplies it) to a double changes x by |L| times 2^-53. The largest |L| at a nonzero, normal quantile on this grid is 691.3 (a = 0.01, p = 1e-3, x = 5.7e-301), so up to 7.7e-14 is unavoidable; 2e-13 allows 2.6x that and matches t_ppf. SciPy's worst error at the points it gets within tolerance is 1.1e-13 (a = 0.01, p = 0.01); it fails 6 points: 4.2e-12 to 4.7e-6 off at p = 5e-324 for a >= 100, and 4.7e-11 off at a = 1e6, p = 1e-10"},"grid":"a in {0.01, 0.1, 0.5, 1, 1.5, 2, 3, 5, 10, 20, 50, 100, 1e3, 1e4, 1e5, 1e6} x p in {0, 5e-324, 1e-300, 1e-100, 1e-50, 1e-20, 1e-10, 1e-5, 1e-3, 0.01, 0.05, 0.1, 0.25, 0.4, 1/2 - 1e-10, 1/2, 1/2 + 1e-10, 0.6, 0.75, 0.9, 0.95, 0.99, 0.999, and the doubles nearest 1 - 1e-5, 1 - 1e-10, 1 - 1e-15, 1}; the quantile is 0 at p = 0 (the end of the support) and p = 1 is tagged pole (+inf); for small a the lower-tail quantiles are below the smallest double","mpmath":{"version":"1.4.1","dps":[50,100]},"scipy":{"version":"1.18.1","function":"scipy.stats.gamma.ppf"},"numpy":"2.5.4","python":"3.13"}
